1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,630
JAKE: Hello, Junior Cycle camp, Jake speaking.

2
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:11,300
WOMAN: Hi. I'm calling for some information about the cycle camp

3
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,890
I'm thinking of sending my son.

4
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:20,353
JAKE: Great. Well, it's held every weekday morning over the summer vacation

5
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:25,200
and we focus on basic cycling skills and safety.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:31,000
We have eight levels for children from three years upwards.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,280
How old's your son?

8
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,610
WOMAN: Charlie? He's seven.

9
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:38,020
He can ride a bike

10
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:43,140
but he needs a little more training before he's safe to go on the road.

11
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:46,910
JAKE: He'd probably be best in Level 5.

12
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:51,520
They start off practising on the site here

13
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,871
and we aim to get them riding on the road,

14
00:00:54,871 --> 00:01:00,620
but first they're taken to ride in the park, away from the traffic.

15
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:06,430
WOMAN: Right. And can you tell me a bit about the instructors?

16
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:12,000
JAKE: Well, all our staff wear different coloured shirts.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,510
So, we have three supervisors, and they have red shirts.

18
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:23,690
They support the instructors, and they also stand in for me if I'm not around.

19
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:29,780
Then the instructors themselves are in blue shirts

20
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:34,090
and one of these is responsible for each class.

21
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,340
WOMAN: OK.

22
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:38,060
JAKE: In order to be accepted

23
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:44,150
all our instructors have to submit a reference from someone

24
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:46,160
who's seen them work with children

25
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:52,410
like if they've worked as a babysitter, for example.

26
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:56,188
Then they have to complete our training course,

27
00:01:56,188 --> 00:01:59,160
including how to do lesson plans

28
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:04,690
and generally care for the well-being of the kids in their class.

29
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:08,000
They do a great job, I have to say.

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
WOMAN: Right. And tell me a bit about the classes.

31
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,350
What size will Charlie's class be?

32
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:21,065
JAKE: We have a limit of eight children in each class,

33
00:02:21,847 --> 00:02:25,860
so their instructor really gets to know them well

34
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:31,724
They're out riding most of the time but they have quiet times too,

35
00:02:31,724 --> 00:02:38,491
where their instructor might tell them a story that's got something to do with cycling,

36
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:42,100
or get them to play a game together.

37
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,830
It's a lot of fun.

38
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:49,820
WOMAN: It must be. Now, what happens if there's rain?

39
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,450
Do the classes still run?

40
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:56,400
JAKE: Oh yes. We don't let that put us off

41
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:00,860
we just put on our waterproofs and keep cycling.

42
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:09,360
WOMAN: And is there anything special Charlie should bring along with him?

43
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:16,420
JAKE: Well, maybe some spare clothes, especially if the weather's not so good.

44
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:20,230
And a snack for break time.

45
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:23,350
WOMAN: How about a drink?

46
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:24,770
JAKE: No, we'll provide that.

47
00:03:24,770 --> 00:03:29,070
And make sure he has shoes, not sandals.

48
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:37,620
WOMAN: Sure. And just at present Charlie has to take medication every few hours

49
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,220
so I'll make sure he has that.

50
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:45,000
JAKE: Absolutely. Just give us details of

51
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,550
when he has to take it and we'll make sure he does.

52
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:49,640
WOMAN: Thanks.

53
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:55,780
JAKE: Now, there are a few things you should know about Day 1 of the camp.

54
00:03:55,780 --> 00:04:01,080
The classes normally start at 9.30 every morning

55
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:07,020
but on Day 1 you should aim to get Charlie here by 9.20.

56
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:12,360
The finishing time will be 12.30 as usual.

57
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:19,170
We need the additional time because there are a few extra things to do.

58
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:29,590
The most important is that we have a very careful check to make sure that every child's helmet fits properly.

59
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:33,300
If it doesn't fit, we'll try to adjust it,

60
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:40,720
or we'll find him another one - but he must wear it all the time he's on the bike.

61
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,410
WOMAN: Of course.

62
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:48,609
JAKE: Then after that, all the instructors will be waiting to meet their classes,

63
00:04:48,609 --> 00:04:53,480
and they'll meet up in the tent - you can't miss it.

64
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:59,100
And each instructor will take their class away and get started.

65
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:03,330
WOMAN: OK. Well that all sounds good.

66
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:09,090
Now can you tell me how much the camp costs a week?

67
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:12,830
JAKE: One hundred ninety-nine dollars.

68
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:18,760
We've managed to keep the price more or less the same as last year

69
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:21,500
it was one hundred ninety then.

70
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:25,680
But the places are filling up quite quickly.

71
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:31,000
WOMAN: Right. OK, well I'd like to book for...
